ow pressurized fuel to leak out, increasing the risk of a fire.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will replace the fuel pump, if necessary, and install a fuel pump cover, free of charge.  The recall began March 14, 2019.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  The recall number for this recall is Q3V.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":106683,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V053000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":3,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"16V888000","received":"2016-12-09","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"ELECTRICAL SYSTEM:WIRING","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain model year 2017 Ridgeline AWD vehicles manufactured April 1, 2016, to August 11, 2016.  Water may enter the rear wiring harness through the connector located under the truck bed drain hole, possibly causing the connection terminals to corrode.","consequence":"Corrosion of the wiring harness can cause increased electrical resistance, unexpectedly activating the vehicle stability assist (VSA) system, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the rear wiring harness and related components, replacing them as necessary, free of charge.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is KD3.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":9179,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=16V888000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"20E068000","received":"2020-09-17","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"EQUIPMENT","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling all Honda Genuine Accessory Tonneau Covers, part number 08Z07-T6Z-100F, sold for installation on 2017-2020 Ridgeline trucks.  If the tonneau cover is not properly secured in the open or closed position, wind resistance may cause the cover to flip and buckle.  If this occurs, the hinges between the center and rear panel may deform, possibly allowing the rear panel to separate from the vehicle.","consequence":"A separated panel may become a road hazard, increasing the risk of crash or injury.","remedy":"Honda will notify all registered owners of 2017-2020 Honda Ridgelines, and dealers will install tethers onto any Honda Genuine Accessory Tonneau Cover to prevent panel separation and apply warning labels, free of charge.  In addition, an updated accessory user's information manual will be provided.  The recall began October 26, 2020.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is F8M.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":151343,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=20E068000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":5,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"9999","make":"HONDA","model":"HARD TONNEAU COVERS"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"21V932000","received":"2021-11-29","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"STRUCTURE:BODY:HOOD","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2019 Passport, 2016-2019 Pilot, and 2017-2020 Ridgeline vehicles.  The hood latch striker may become damaged and separate from the hood, which can result in the hood opening while driving.","consequence":"A hood that opens while driving can obstruct the driver's view and increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will either repair the hood latch striker, or replace the hood if necessary, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed January 18, 2022.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is PBV.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":724826,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=21V932000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":9,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"22V867000","received":"2022-11-23","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"BACK OVER PREVENTION: SENSING SYSTEM: CAMERA","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2017-2019 Ridgeline vehicles.  Opening and closing the tailgate may break the rearview camera wiring harness, causing the rearview camera to fail.","consequence":"An inoperative rearview camera can reduce the driver's rear visibility, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the rearview camera wiring harness, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed August 31, 2023.  Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is 6RW.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":117445,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=22V867000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":3,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V751000","received":"2023-11-13","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"ENGINE AND ENGINE COOLING:ENGINE:HARD PARTS INTERNAL/MECHANICAL","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2015-2020 Acura TLX, 2016-2020 Acura MDX, 2016 and 2018-2019 Pilot, 2017 and 2019 Ridgeline, and 2018-2019 Odyssey vehicles.  Due to a manufacturing error, the connecting rod bearing in the engine may wear and seize, damaging the engine.","consequence":"A damaged engine may run improperly or stall while driving, increasing the risk of a fire, crash, or injury.","remedy":"Dealers will inspect and repair, or replace the engine as necessary, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed March 28, 2024. 2016-2017 Acura MDX owner letters were mailed November 1, 2024.  2016-2020 Acura MDX owner letters are expected to be mailed in mid-December 2024. Honda began mailing owner notification letters as of March 18, 2024. 2015-2016 Acura owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-December 2024, 2018 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed the end of March/early April 2024, 2019 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-May 2024, 2020 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-June 2024, and 2016-2020 Acura MDX owner letters are expected to be mailed January 27, 2025.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for these recalls are XG1 and GG0.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":248999,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V751000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":18,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2015","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V858000","received":"2023-12-19","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail.","consequence":"Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the fuel pump module, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed September 6, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are KGC and KGD.  This recall is an expansion of NHTSA recall numbers 21V-215 and 20V-314.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2490460,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V858000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":107,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"FIT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"26V332000","received":"2026-05-22","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018-2021, 2023 Acura TLX, 2019-2024 RDX, 2017-2020, 2022-2026 MDX, 2017-2021, 2023, 2025 Honda Ridgeline, 2017-2022 Pilot, 2019-2021 Passport, 2018-2026 Odyssey, 2019-2022 Insight, 2019-2021 HR-V, 2018-2020 Fit, 2020-2022 CR-V Hybrid, 2017-2022 CR-V, 2017-2018, 2021 Civic Type R, 2017-2021 Civic hatchback, 2016-2020 Civic coupe, 2016-2022 Civic, 2017-2022 Accord Hybrid, and 2016-2022 Accord vehicles. The front passenger seat weight sensor may crack and short circuit, which can cause the air bags to deploy unintentionally during a crash.","consequence":"Air bags that deploy unintentionally during a crash increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the seat weight sensors, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed July 7, 2026. Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138. Honda's numbers for this recall are BOL, WO9, OOA, WOM, XOH, NOC, POD, BOE, UOF, POB, EOG, AOI, QO8, TOJ, DO7, and SOK. This recall expands previous NHTSA recall number 24V064. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall will be searchable on NHTSA.gov beginning May 29, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":98892,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V332000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":92,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2022","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC TYPE R"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVIC TYPE R"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"26V365000","received":"2026-06-04","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"STRUCTURE:FRAME AND MEMBERS","summary":"American Honda Motor Company (Honda) is recalling certain 2016-2022 Honda Pilot, 2017-2023 Ridgeline, 2019-2023 Passport, and 2014-2020 Acura MDX vehicles that were sold in Connecticut, Delaware, District of Columbia, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kentucky, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Vermont, Virginia, West Virginia, or Wisconsin. The rear subframe may corrode at the suspension mounting points, which can result in rear suspension component failure.","consequence":"Failure of rear suspension components, such as the rear control arm, can cause a loss of vehicle handling and control, increasing the risk of a crash or injury.","remedy":"Dealers will inspect the rear subframe and install a rear subframe reinforcement kit and, as necessary, repair or replace the rear subframe components, free of charge. Owner letters were mailed November 5, 2026. Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138. Honda's numbers for this recall are AOU and AOT. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall will become searchable on NHTSA.gov beginning June 10, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":965561,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V365000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":26,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2023","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2015","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2022","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2023","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2014","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true}]}
